<span id="profiles-title" class="anchor-alias" aria-hidden="true"></span><span
  id="profiles-close-title"
  class="anchor-alias"
  aria-hidden="true"></span>
<section
  class="feature-copy-grid feature-copy-grid--top"
  aria-labelledby="profiles-section-0"
>
  <div>
    <p class="section-kicker">separate identities</p><h2
      id="profiles-section-0"
    >
      Sign into the same site in different profiles.
    </h2>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-copy-list">
    <article>
      <h3>Start with Personal</h3><p>
        Personal is permanent and keeps your existing Blanc data. In Settings,
        name another profile and choose Create profile window.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Keep browsing data separate</h3><p>
        Named profiles isolate cookies, site data, Favorites, history, download
        metadata, and remembered permissions. Their ordinary and private
        sessions are separate from other profiles.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Open more than one window</h3><p>
        Each native window owns its tabs, groups, Island panel, and Recently
        Closed list. Saved windows return to their associated profile after
        relaunch.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
<figure class="product-capture feature-capture released-capture">
  <a
    href="/feature-captures/profile-window.png"
    aria-label="View the separate Studio profile window"
    ><img
      src="/feature-captures/profile-window.png"
      width="1440"
      height="900"
      loading="lazy"
      decoding="async"
      alt="A separate Studio profile window with an empty tab set and no Personal Favorites."
    /></a
  >
  <figcaption>
    The Studio profile opens its own window without Personal’s tabs or
    Favorites. Device-level preferences and blocking totals remain shared.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
<section class="feature-copy-grid" aria-labelledby="profiles-section-1">
  <div>
    <p class="section-kicker">what is shared</p><h2 id="profiles-section-1">
      A profile is a browsing identity on this device.
    </h2>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-copy-list">
    <article>
      <h3>Device preferences stay consistent</h3><p>
        Appearance, network and privacy preferences, usage-measurement choices,
        and Patron status remain shared across the device.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Sync belongs to Personal</h3><p>
        Sync is available only to Personal. Creating a named profile does not
        create another synced identity.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Delete deliberately</h3><p>
        Deleting a named profile requires its exact name. It closes that
        profile’s windows and removes its browsing data and saved workspaces.
        Files you downloaded remain on disk; Personal cannot be deleted.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
<aside class="truth-note" aria-labelledby="profiles-note-title">
  <p class="section-kicker">good to know</p><h2 id="profiles-note-title">
    Separate site data, not separate operating-system users.
  </h2>
  <p>
    Profiles separate browsing identities inside Blanc. They are not
    password-protected vaults or a security boundary against someone who can use
    your device account. Named profile data stays on this device.
  </p>
  <a
    class="text-link"
    href="/support#sync"
    data-track="feature_cta_click"
    data-feature="profiles"
    data-cta-position="related-feature"
    >See what Personal can sync <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
  >
</aside>
